====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[flip]] over onto the [[back]] or [[top]]; to turn [[upside down]].
#* '''1919''', Iowa Highway Commission, Service Bulletin, Issues 15-32, page 48
#*: Were speeding when car '''turtled''' {{...}}Auto crashed into curb and '''turtled'''.
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To move along slowly.
#* '''2012''', Sophie B. Watson, ''Cadillac Couches'' (page 193)
#*: We '''turtled''' along in Manitoba, back into the heart of the prairies.
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[turn]] and [[swim]] [[upside down]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2009|author=Amy Waeschle|title=Chasing Waves: A Surfer's Tale of Obsessive Wandering|page=149|passage=I '''turtled''' my board beneath it, flipped upright, and started paddling again.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[hunt]] turtles, especially in the water.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1973|author=Bernard Nietschmann|title=Between Land and Water: The Subsistence Ecology of the Miskito Indians|page=153|passage=Of these, 80 '''turtled''' (65%), 26 hunted and '''turtled''' (20%), and 18 hunted (15%).}}
# {{lb|en|video games|board games}} To build up a large [[defense]] force and strike only occasionally, rather than going for an offensive strategy.

